{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c383","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b081-544e-74f2-a0d1-9b009342eb06"},"sequence":28,"recorded_at":1780531400000051,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"dae84e08-92bc-496b-b7d3-463fd560ae23","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"dae84e08-92bc-496b-b7d3-463fd560ae23","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"dae84e08-92bc-496b-b7d3-463fd560ae23"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b081-6a79-7f11-9c76-6310a870cafe"},"task_id":"01a0b081-6a79-7f11-9c76-6310a870cafe","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b081-6a79-7f11-9c76-6310a870cafe","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-1-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260830-219okr, status=development)' 2>&1; echo EXIT:$?\\ncat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_producer.md\\necho \\\"---BOARD_DIR---\\\"; echo $TASK_BOARD_DIR; pwd; git rev-parse HEAD 2>&1; git status --short 2>&1 | head -n 50\",\n  \"description\": \"Set status and read producer brief\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"primary\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"status_changed\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"to-review\\\"},\\\"side_effects\\\":[{\\\"action\\\":\\\"escalated\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"STORY-260830-4qojoz\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"to-review\\\"},{\\\"action\\\":\\\"escalated\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"EPIC-260830-3v9jlg\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"to-review\\\"}]}}\\nEXIT:0\\nOwn TASK-260830-219okr (implement-dual-stack-major-negotiation), first leaf of STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation, EPIC M2; sibling 19bjfj follows). Landed owners you build on: internal/rpcwire (RPC 2/3/4/5 envelopes, hello maps, namespaces, contract profiles, limits, Structured Error framing statically bound per major) and internal/hostchannel (Host Channel 1.0.0 / RPC 5 authenticated endpoint) from STORY-260830-1kiyj6, plus the Config-4 selection in internal/config. Implement, as production code, major negotiation under the pinned Sections 11.2-11.3 (framing/handshake, hello as the first request, request_id echo, closed operation registry), 11.8/11.9 (RPC 3 directory-capable and RPC 4 TerminalBackend-evidence majors; a v3 node negotiating v2 performs core sync only and exposes the peer as directory_mesh_unsupported, never as zero inventory; the same shape for RPC 4 backend-evidence activation), 11.10.1 (RPC 5 on the Config-4 host channel with contracts.rpc [\\\"5.0.0\\\"] only) and 17.1-17.4 (compatibility: unsupported majors, unknown closed fields/tags fail closed; RPC 3 and 2 dual-stack for at least one stable release; legacy RPC 2/3/4 dual-stack obligations apply only to explicitly legacy installations and never require a Config-4 endpoint to accept legacy — no byte sniffing, extension field, argv value, environment value or failed handshake can select a fallback; Section 6.6): a negotiator that, given the local installation's configuration generation and the peer's hello, selects exactly one common major or refuses no-common-major with the pinned Section 15 class (incompatible_protocol, exit 6, only when incompatibility is actually known), preserves core-only peers (RPC 2 core sync, unsupported directory/backend activation exposed explicitly as directory_mesh_unsupported / the RPC 4 equivalent, never as zero inventory or a capability claim), never downgrades a Config-4 host-channel endpoint below RPC 5 and never substitutes negotiation for the hostchannel admission (identity equality, allowlist, generation) that TASK-260830-z1yxg9 owns; for explicitly legacy installations select the highest common major among 2/3/4 with the exact per-major contract keys (RPC 2: 14 contracts/6 namespaces; RPC 3: 24 keys/7 namespaces; RPC 4: 25 keys/8 namespaces; RPC 5: RPC 4 shapes with protocol_version 5.0.0) and the historically bound Structured Error version per major; refuse a v2 bound inside a v3+ frame and any cross-major mixing. Tests: drive the negotiator with every pair (local majors × peer hello majors) as a table derived from the pinned text, positives for each admitted selection, negatives for no-common-major, mixed-major frames, a Config-4 endpoint offered legacy, a legacy installation offered RPC 5 only, sniffing/fallback attempts (byte sniffing, extension field, argv, env, failed handshake), and the core-only exposure invariant (a core-only peer's inventory is reported as unsupported activation, not empty); every gate a narrowing mutant; the peer-visible outcomes must be pure data (no capability advertised).\\nCOMMON CONTRACT (first leaf of a Story on trunk 7efe385 or later). Normative authority: the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md headings named below; the v0.7.0 adoption (STORY-260916-3uqbwq) is landing during your run and is byte-identical in these sections — if it has landed when you refresh, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers. Reuse the landed owners (canonicaljson closed shapes, scalar, sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate, fencing, sessprofile, provhost/resumesmoke, hosttrust/peeridentity/sshtransport, rpcwire/hostchannel, sessadapter, terminalbackend, localstore, secprim/secconftest) — never fork a second model; extend or adopt. Traceability: do NOT edit internal/traceability (ownership registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) in this first leaf — the Story's FINAL leaf carries the registry bindings and re-pin once the v0.7.0 registry is on trunk; document your clause coverage in a package-local TRACEABILITY.md and the conformance matrix instead. Evidence