as production code, major negotiation under the pinned Sections 11.2-11.3 (framing/handshake, hello as the first request, request_id echo, closed operation registry), 11.8/11.9 (RPC 3 directory-capable and RPC 4 TerminalBackend-evidence majors; a v3 node negotiating v2 performs core sync only and exposes the peer as directory_mesh_unsupported, never as zero inventory; the same shape for RPC 4 backend-evidence activation), 11.10.1 (RPC 5 on the Config-4 host channel with contracts.rpc [\\\"5.0.0\\\"] only) and 17.1-17.4 (compatibility: unsupported majors, unknown closed fields/tags fail closed; RPC 3 and 2 dual-stack for at least one stable release; legacy RPC 2/3/4 dual-stack obligations apply only to explicitly legacy installations and never require a Config-4 endpoint to accept legacy — no byte sniffing, extension field, argv value, environment value or failed handshake can select a fallback; Section 6.6): a negotiator that, given the local installation's configuration generation and the peer's hello, selects exactly one common major or refuses no-common-major with the pinned Section 15 class (incompatible_protocol, exit 6, only when incompatibility is actually known), preserves core-only peers (RPC 2 core sync, unsupported directory/backend activation exposed explicitly as directory_mesh_unsupported / the RPC 4 equivalent, never as zero inventory or a capability claim), never downgrades a Config-4 host-channel endpoint below RPC 5 and never substitutes negotiation for the hostchannel admission (identity equality, allowlist, generation) that TASK-260830-z1yxg9 owns; for explicitly legacy installations select the highest common major among 2/3/4 with the exact per-major contract keys (RPC 2: 14 contracts/6 namespaces; RPC 3: 24 keys/7 namespaces; RPC 4: 25 keys/8 namespaces; RPC 5: RPC 4 shapes with protocol_version 5.0.0) and the historically bound Structured Error version per major; refuse a v2 bound inside a v3+ frame and any cross-major mixing. Tests: drive the negotiator with every pair (local majors × peer hello majors) as a table derived from the pinned text, positives for each admitted=== review verdict search ===\\nunknown shorthand flag: 'l' in -l\\nUsage:\\n  task-board [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  admin                  Server administration (users, tokens, access)\\n  boards                 List boards accessible to the current user (remote mode)\\n  claude                 Launch Claude through the Task-board Session Manager\\n  codex                  Attach Codex to the Task-board Session Manager\\n  completion             Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell\\n  export                 Export current board into a tar.gz archive\\n  goal                   Read and align the board-scoped parent primary goal\\n  grep                   Full-text search across board files\\n  handoff                Verify role handoff evidence and move to the role end status\\n  help                   Help about any command\\n  import                 Import a tar.gz archive into the current board\\n  init                   Install task-board project integrations\\n  limits                 Inspect and control provider rate-limit state\\n  login                  Store a token for the current remote\\n  logout                 Remove active user's token for current remote\\n  m                      Execute a mutation (write operation)\\n  migrate-keychain       Import legacy remote credentials into macOS Keychain\\n  migrate-project-config Preview or apply guarded deprecated project-config alias migration\\n  plan                   Show execution plan with phases and critical path\\n  q                      Query the board with a mini DSL\\n  repair-links           List or remove unsupported container dependency links\\n  resource               Upload, update, download, and delete board resources\\n  self-update            Update task-board to the latest version\\n  session                Inspect and stop Task-board Session Manager sessions\\n  spawn                  Queue an agent spawn run for a board task\\n  switch-user            Switch active user for current remote\\n  tree                   Show board as hierarchical t\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5030,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1258,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
