duction `negotiate.go`, 2 test files, `mutations.py`, README, TRACEABILITY) plus README/LOGBOOK additions.\\\\n\\\\n**This run's work (successor after rev1 CR validation stopped at command 5/27):**\\\\n\\\\n- Root-caused the blocker: `internal/sessquery` hit the default 10m `go test` timeout under `-race` (600.336s in CR validation). Proved independent of this leaf — sessquery's test binary doesn't link meshneg (`go list -deps -test` count 0), meshneg has no `init()`/I/O/shared state — and proved timeout-only: with `-timeout 20m` sessquery passes green, exit 0, 617.983s, no failures or race reports. Machine load was 20–42 on 16 CPUs. No sessquery file touched (outside story boundary); full suite reruns automatically on CR construction.\\\\n- Re-verified the leaf: meshneg tests ok (15 top-level, 145 PASS lines), `-race -cover` ok at 87.8%, mutant harness exit 0 with a `results.json` tally of 27 killed / neutral passed / harmless control survived, gofmt clean, `go build`/`go vet ./...` clean, owner packages (`rpcwire`, `axerror`) and adjacent (`hostchannel`, `config`) green, spec bindings (`directory_mesh_unsupported` @1.2.0, `terminal_backend_unavailable` @1.3.0, pin `0cbdf100`) confirmed verbatim in SPEC.v0.6.0.\\\\n- Fixed one real defect found: prose claimed \\\\\\\"28 narrowing probes\\\\\\\" but the harness defines 27 narrowing + neutral + control (confirmed in rev1's own `results.json`); corrected in both READMEs, LOGBOOK, and evidence. Production code untouched.\\\\n- Updated board outcomes: `TASK-260830-219okr_results.md`, `TASK-260830-219okr_conformance-matrix.md` (11 of 11 AC rows driven, call sites + mutants), and a real gzip evidence tar (127 entries: fresh meshneg logs, full mutant per-plant output, sessquery 20m pass log + analysis note).\\\\n\\\\nNo `refresh-candidate` needed (`origin/main` == base `7efe385`). No directives were recorded for the run.\\\",\\\"reason\\\":null}}\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 36800,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 9200,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
