{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ce79","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b081-544e-74f2-a0d1-9b009342eb06"},"sequence":1431,"recorded_at":1780531400002857,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"dae84e08-92bc-496b-b7d3-463fd560ae23","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"dae84e08-92bc-496b-b7d3-463fd560ae23","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"dae84e08-92bc-496b-b7d3-463fd560ae23"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0a302fa72e58b2d3859508eb7e3","text":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-17\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-219okr — dual-stack major negotiation (first leaf)\n9|- DELIVERED: `internal/meshneg` (`Negotiate`/`LocalMajors`/`PeerOffer`/`Select` over `Refusal`/`Decision` pure data): generation-to-majors mapping (Config-1: 2; Config-2: 2,3; Config-3: 2,3,4; Config-4: exactly 5), single-major peer-offer validation against the framing major, highest-common selection, no-common-major refusal with registry-resolved `incompatible_protocol`/6 (unknown config: `invalid_config`/3), exact per-major contracts/namespaces/bound error versions rebuilt from rpcwire/axerror, and core-only peer exposure (`directory_mesh_unsupported`, `terminal_backend_unavailable`), never zero inventory. Frames nothing, admits nothing, pure/stateless. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n10|- BINDING CHOICE: the RPC-4 exposure equivalent is the registered `terminal_backend_unavailable` (exit 6), not a minted token — Section 11.9 requires reporting evidence unsupported rather than empty and 17.4 requires reporting activation unavailable; the 1.3.0 exit-6 row carries exactly that code. Refusal/exposure exits resolve via `axerror.ExitCodeFor` under each code's introducing version; cross-version stability is asserted by test, not assumed.\n11|- MUTANTS: 27 narrowing probes killed by named tests (neutral passed, harmless Detail-text control SURVIVED as designed; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`). Two initial SURVIVEDs were test gaps the harness caught: substituted-keys (same count, caught by membership loop, not length check) and peer-mixing-1-beside-common (unobservable without overlap) — both closed with new cases before the evidence run. Successor run RUN-260917-244f06 re-executed the harness: 27 killed, neutral passed, control SURVIVED (exit 0), and corrected the earlier \"28\" count.\n12|- BOUNDS: v2 1-16 minor ranges select the major only (within-major minor selection future work); handshake sequencing stays with rpcwire decode + the responder; admission (identity/allowlist/generation) stays with TASK-260830-z1yxg9 with separation pinned by `TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission`; no `ax` command, doctor result, or capability claimed. Traceability registry/digest untouched for the story final leaf (package-local TRACEABILITY.md only).\n13|- AC: 11 of 11 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence).\n14|\n15|### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\n16|- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\n17|- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\n18|- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\n19|- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\n20|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\n21|- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\n22|- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\n23|- 2026-09-17 rev3 on `fc67abd`: pin `d3eca906…`, report 132 cases / 65 bindings / 7 unowned / 49 of 535 clauses; harness denominator 24 prior + 9 new; refresh-candidate completed.\n24|\n25|### TASK-260830-2atgj4 — property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
